    "id": "x4_primitive_shiftpair_zero_fold_norm_divisibility",
    "title": "Primitive shift-pair zero-fold norm divisibility",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a balanced signed shift-pair polynomial C, beta_a=0 exactly when Phi_(n_a) divides C in Z[X], while X-1 always divides C. If S and Z are the active and zero prefix-supplied dyadic levels, then 2^(|S|+sum_(j in S,a in Z)min(n_j,n_a)/2) p^R_S divides the product of active cyclotomic norms. Together with the shared Haar ceiling this gives the exact necessary pattern inequality 2^(|S|+T_2) p^R_S A_S^A_S<=(eN)^A_S. This can exclude zero-heavy patterns but supplies no ownership or population bound.",
